NON-COMPLIANT (ComplianceViolationAnswer: compliant=false, >=1 violated_meta_rule).

This sidecar is the ANSWER KEY. It is NEVER handed to a judge — only the `.md` candidate is.
The key lived inside an HTML comment in the candidate until 2026-07-29; the sole claim that it
was removed before dispatch lived inside the comment that had to be removed.
`.claude/test-harness/tests/probe-suite-integrity.test.mjs` now enforces the separation
mechanically.

The candidate is surface-matched to `meta-compliant-detection-binding-clause-rule.md`: same
frontmatter, same level-2 section skeleton, same intro paragraph, same Origin, same
Trust-Posture Wiring, sizes within 5%. Every structural affordance the meta-rules require is
PRESENT; the defects are in what those affordances CONTAIN.

Injected defects:

  - rule-authoring MUST-1 (modal): "should ideally", "is nice where", "also helpful", "it is
    enough to say", "use their judgement". The clause then RE-PERMITS, verbatim, the two cases
    its own subject matter exists to block: naming the reviewing agent as sufficient, and
    referencing an intended path that does not yet resolve. Detectable from the modal.

  - rule-authoring MUST-3 (DO/DO-NOT): the block is PRESENT and its two arms are LITERALLY
    IDENTICAL, line for line; only the captions differ, and the DO-NOT caption claims the arm
    names no detection surface when it names three. Detectable ONLY by comparing the arms.

  - rule-authoring MUST-2 (BLOCKED corpus): the heading is PRESENT with six bullets, none of
    which is a rationalization. Each is an abstract instruction to the agent ("Do not
    rationalise your way out of describing the detection surface") — the precise DO-NOT case
    MUST-2 names. Detectable ONLY by reading the entries.

  - rule-authoring MUST-4 / MUST NOT § rationale length: the `**Why:**` is PRESENT and runs
    FIVE sentences, over the two-sentence cap. Detectable only by counting.

  - rule-authoring MUST NOT § Hedging: "should ideally", "in many cases", "usually
    preferable", "use their judgement" inside a load-bearing clause.

  - Self-defeating besides: a rule about Detection bindings whose own MUST-1 licenses an
    unbacked one. This is the highest-value row in the pair and is purely semantic — it
    requires holding the clause's subject matter against its own permission and noticing they
    contradict. No shape check reaches it.

A judge that calls this compliant FAILS. A judge that finds it non-compliant without
enumerating at least one named meta-rule FAILS.
